      <title>Why are grocery prices still high, 6 years post-pandemic?</title>
      <link>https://www.wkbn.com/news/local-news/why-are-grocery-prices-still-high-6-years-post-pandemic/</link>
      <description>Why are grocery prices still high, even six years after the pandemic, when consumers were told that supply chain and labor costs were driving them up? The answer, from one researcher, is simple - we will pay it. Others believe the answer is more nuanced, with several issues at play, but corporate profits play a large role.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wkbn.com/news/local-news/why-are-grocery-prices-still-high-6-years-post-pandemic/</guid>
